    "title": "Wanganui gardener jailed for child sex abuse images",
    "byline": "",
    "pub_date": "2009-04-07",
    "body": "On 6 April 2009 in the Wanganui District Court a 53-year-old gardener of Wanganui was sentenced to two years imprisonment on two charges of distribution and possession of objectionable publications. The images were child sex abuse images. In 2008 he had also downloaded objectionable material on a laptop while on home detention after being released from prison on a charge relating to grooming a 14-year-old girl."
  },
  {
    "source_url": "https://www.dia.govt.nz/press.nsf/d77da9b523f12931cc256ac5000d19b6/a480b170f8b6bdc3cc257591001ce201!OpenDocument",
    "mode": "resolved",
    "title": "Burwood man jailed for possessing objectionable images",
    "byline": "",
    "pub_date": "2009-04-07",
    "body": "On 7 April 2009 a customer service representative, 26, of Burwood, was sentenced in the Christchurch District Court to 18 months in prison on 18 charges of possessing an objectionable publication. His computer system contained some 4000 objectionable images of child sex abuse."
  },
  {
    "source_url": "https://www.dia.govt.nz/press.nsf/d77da9b523f12931cc256ac5000d19b6/a480b170f8b6bdc3cc257591001ce201!OpenDocument",
    "mode": "resolved",
    "title": "Christchurch man sentenced to home detention for child sex abuse images",
    "byline": "",
    "pub_date": "2009-04-07",
    "body": "On 3 April 2009 in the Christchurch District Court a contract supervisor, 46, of Christchurch, was sentenced to eight months home detention with special conditions and 160 hours of community work on 29 charges relating to possession or distribution of child sex abuse images."
  },
  {
    "source_url": "https://www.dia.govt.nz/press.nsf/d77da9b523f12931cc256ac5000d19b6/bfe7914bcab262f5cc2575a800160f5b!OpenDocument",
    "mode": "resolved",
    "title": "75-year-old jailed for child sexual abuse images",
    "byline": "",
    "pub_date": "2009-04-30",
    "body": "On 29 April 2009 a 75-year-old retired man of Christchurch was jailed for two years on 27 charges of possessing or distributing objectionable images, mainly of young boys in sexual poses or acts."
  },
  {
    "source_url": "https://www.dia.govt.nz/press.nsf/d77da9b523f12931cc256ac5000d19b6/bfe7914bcab262f5cc2575a800160f5b!OpenDocument",
    "mode": "resolved",
    "title": "Former teacher jailed for grooming children online",
    "byline": "",
    "pub_date": "2009-04-30",
    "body": "On 30 April 2009 a 60-year-old former teacher of Kaiapoi was sentenced to two-and-a-half years prison in the Christchurch District Court after a jury found him guilty on 24 charges of making or possessing objectionable publications, on-line chat logs in which he groomed and manipulated young girls into performing sexual acts. A mother complained about an online discussion her 11 year old daughter was engaged in. The prosecutor suggested six years imprisonment as an appropriate sentencing starting point."
  },
