    "title": "Man sentenced to 4 years for possessing child sexual exploitation material",
    "byline": "",
    "pub_date": "2025-10-10",
    "body": "On 8 October 2025 at the Manukau District Court, 41-year-old Visen Keo was sentenced to 4 years imprisonment. He pled guilty to four charges related to possessing over 50,000 objectionable images depicting the sexual exploitation and abuse of babies and children. Three of these charges were representative. Forensic analysis found 54,979 unique objectionable publications, including babies."
  },
  {
    "source_url": "https://www.dia.govt.nz/press.nsf/d77da9b523f12931cc256ac5000d19b6/90d13a596343e0a8cc258d1f00140215!OpenDocument",
    "mode": "resolved",
    "title": "Man sentenced to 12 months home detention for child sexual exploitation material",
    "byline": "",
    "pub_date": "2025-10-10",
    "body": "On 9 October 2025 at the Invercargill District Court, 62-year-old Steven Bruce Cook was sentenced to 12 months home detention for distributing and possessing objectionable material. The sentencing Judge adopted a starting point of 4 years and 6 months imprisonment before applying discounts totalling 55%. He possessed 6,240 child sexual exploitation and abuse files. Victims ranged in age from babies to young people under the age of 16."
  },
